# /sdd-map

Purpose:
  Map prompts to tasks and subtasks. Reads prompts from
  prompts/inbox/ (or accepts --prompt), classifies each to a
  chain arm via keyword matching, derives tasks (T-NNN) and
  subtasks (DB, BE, API, FE, MD, DC, Test), and prints the
  mapping in formatted output.

Usage:
  /sdd-map
  /sdd-map --prompt "<text>"
  /sdd-map --json

Options:
  --prompt <text>   Map a single inline prompt instead of inbox
  --json            Output machine-readable JSON
  --chain-arm <arm> Filter to a specific chain arm (P1|D1|S1|C1|R1|DEP1)

Mode: READ_ONLY

InitialLoad:
  - .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd (routing)
  - .sdd/chains/selector.sdd (arm map)
  - .sdd/chains/dl2-decision.sdd (P-TK/P-ST stages)
  - .sdd/commands/sdd-intents.sdd (ChainArmMapping keywords)
  - prompts/inbox/ (source prompts)

ChainArmMapping (reused from sdd-intents.sdd):
  "write / plan / design / document" -> D1 (Documentation)
  "implement / code / build / develop" -> C1 (Code Generation)
  "review / audit / test / verify" -> R1 (Review)
  "deploy / release / publish" -> DEP1 (Deploy)
  "analyze / explain / understand" -> P1 (Prompt Analysis)
  "spec / define / model / schema" -> S1 (SDD Generation)

SubtaskTypes:
  DB, BE, API, FE, MD, DC, Test

Output:
  PROMPT-TASK MAP

  Prompt: "<prompt text>"
    Arm:  D1  |  Chain: D0->D1->D0
    Tasks:
      T-001: <generated task title>
        Subtasks:
          ST-001-01 [DB]  ...
          ST-001-02 [BE]  ...
          ST-001-03 [API] ...
          ST-001-04 [FE]  ...
          ST-001-05 [MD]  ...
          ST-001-06 [DC]  ...
          ST-001-07 [Test]...

  Summary:
    Prompts mapped:  N
    Tasks generated:  N
    Subtasks generated: N

Rules:
  [MAP-01] /sdd-map MUST NOT modify any file.
  [MAP-02] Prompt classification MUST use keyword matching as primary signal.
  [MAP-03] Task/subtask IDs are generated placeholders for mapping preview.
  [MAP-04] Unmatched prompts get arm: UNKNOWN and require human review.

